WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.757
"I can't believe you're going to be on TV, Ben," Gaby said on the way home from school.

2
00:00:09.758 --> 00:00:11.833
"You'll be famous!"

3
00:00:11.834 --> 00:00:15.138
Ben frowned. "I don't want to be famous.

4
00:00:15.139 --> 00:00:19.250
I don't even want to be on Kids' Kitchen Showdown

5
00:00:19.251 --> 00:00:27.380
." After Mr. Icky had picked Ben to be on the TV show, everyone was

6
00:00:27.381 --> 00:00:32.183
excited. Winnie had given Ben a big hug. "You'll do

7
00:00:32.184 --> 00:00:36.655
great!" Other monsters patted him on the back and gave him the claws-up

8
00:00:36.656 --> 00:00:41.305
sign. Some monsters even looked a bit

9
00:00:41.306 --> 00:00:44.982
jealous. Gaby was still talking as she and Ben walked

10
00:00:44.983 --> 00:00:47.611
along. "I didn't even know you liked

11
00:00:47.612 --> 00:00:52.423
cooking." "I hate cooking," Ben said. "Mr. Icky made a

12
00:00:52.424 --> 00:00:55.088
mistake. I accidentally made something that tastes

13
00:00:55.089 --> 00:00:58.191
good. But that doesn't mean I know what I'm

14
00:00:58.192 --> 00:01:00.838
doing." "You're being silly," Gaby

15
00:01:00.838 --> 00:01:04.839
said. "You obviously have talent and don't realize

16
00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:08.812
it." "Well, I'm not going to win the competition," Ben went

17
00:01:08.813 --> 00:01:10.405
on. "The judges are

18
00:01:10.406 --> 00:01:19.253
humans. They're going to choose a human cook—not a

19
00:01:19.254 --> 00:01:26.355
monster." That evening Ben sat on his back stoop, trying to distract himself from the cooking

20
00:01:26.356 --> 00:01:30.586
show. He made himself think about possible birthday presents for

21
00:01:30.587 --> 00:01:34.481
Winnie. "What do witches like?" he asked

22
00:01:34.482 --> 00:01:37.080
himself. He thought about Winnie's favorite things.

23
00:01:37.081 --> 00:01:42.896
She loved to fly. Maybe she'd like a new broom?

24
00:01:42.897 --> 00:01:46.153
Ben pulled out his phone.

25
00:01:46.154 --> 00:01:49.980
He found a website that sold flying brooms.

26
00:01:49.981 --> 00:01:53.129
One broom was shaped like a lightning bolt.

27
00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:56.157
Ben watched a demonstration video.

28
00:01:56.158 --> 00:02:01.822
The broom was so fast, it left a streak of fire across the sky.

29
00:02:01.823 --> 00:02:08.626
"Wow!" Ben said. "Winnie would love this broom. How much does it cost?"

30
00:02:08.627 --> 00:02:13.009
He scrolled down the page and found the price.

31
00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:17.536
"Six thousand dollars?" Ben gulped.

32
00:02:17.537 --> 00:02:20.782
There was no way he could afford that.

33
00:02:20.783 --> 00:02:23.919
He looked at some other flying broom websites.

34
00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:27.561
The cheapest broom Ben saw was still too expensive.

35
00:02:27.562 --> 00:02:32.620
It was five hundred dollars, and it looked like a piece of junk.

36
00:02:32.621 --> 00:02:37.350
Ben's shoulders slumped, and he put his phone away.

37
00:02:37.351 --> 00:02:43.430
As Ben brooded, the hedge that ran down the side of his yard shook slightly.

38
00:02:43.431 --> 00:02:48.159
Something was rustling on the ground.

39
00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:50.928
Ben peered over.

40
00:02:50.929 --> 00:02:56.204
"Who's there?" he said. There was no answer.

41
00:02:56.205 --> 00:02:59.163
For a moment the hedge was still.

42
00:02:59.164 --> 00:03:01.635
Then it moved again.

43
00:03:01.636 --> 00:03:05.547
"Something is in there," Ben thought.

44
00:03:05.548 --> 00:03:10.035
He floated over for a closer look.

45
00:03:10.036 --> 00:03:15.265
He moved some of the leaves out of the way and looked in at the branches.

46
00:03:15.266 --> 00:03:18.738
A pair of glowing eyes stared back at him.

47
00:03:18.739 --> 00:03:24.315
A chill ran down Ben's spine. "It's a . . . a kitten!"

48
00:03:24.316 --> 00:03:30.064
Meow! The tiny black kitten leaped out of the hedge and straight toward Ben.

49
00:03:30.065 --> 00:03:31.670
Ben jumped to the side.

50
00:03:31.671 --> 00:03:33.866
The kitten landed on the grass.

51
00:03:33.867 --> 00:03:37.028
It looked up at Ben and hissed.

52
00:03:37.029 --> 00:03:40.817
"Oh, boy," Ben said, glancing around.

53
00:03:40.818 --> 00:03:44.369
A lot of monsters and humans loved cats.

54
00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:47.689
But cats hated ghosts!

55
00:03:47.690 --> 00:03:52.198
Ben ran toward his back door with the kitten chasing him all the way.

56
00:03:52.199 --> 00:03:57.341
"Mom will be furious if this beast gets inside," Ben thought.

57
00:03:57.342 --> 00:04:00.001
He shot across his backyard.

58
00:04:00.002 --> 00:04:05.036
The kitten sprinted behind him, hissing and pouncing at his feet.

59
00:04:05.037 --> 00:04:08.889
Ben floated through his fence and into a neighbor's backyard.

60
00:04:08.890 --> 00:04:11.098
He stopped to catch his breath.

61
00:04:11.099 --> 00:04:13.467
"Whew! I think I lost—"

62
00:04:13.468 --> 00:04:17.524
Hiss! Meow! The kitten was on top of the fence.

63
00:04:17.525 --> 00:04:20.356
It leaped down and fell right through Ben.

64
00:04:20.357 --> 00:04:25.761
"Ahh!" Ben dashed through the neighbor's yard and onto the street.

65
00:04:25.762 --> 00:04:28.490
The kitten was still right behind him.

66
00:04:28.491 --> 00:04:31.842
Ben darted upward, flying over the trees.

67
00:04:31.843 --> 00:04:34.414
Looking down, he saw the kitten.

68
00:04:34.415 --> 00:04:39.255
It was still hissing at him, but at least it couldn't fly.

69
00:04:39.256 --> 00:04:48.310
With a sigh of relief, Ben flew home. On

70
00:04:48.311 --> 00:04:54.849
Wednesday morning Ben was one of the first students to arrive in the cooking classroom. He

71
00:04:54.850 --> 00:05:02.086
saw Mr. Icky pulling pots from one of the cabinets. "Um,

72
00:05:02.087 --> 00:05:07.461
Mr. Icky," Ben said. "Can I talk to you for a second?" Mr.

73
00:05:07.462 --> 00:05:09.986
Icky turned around. "Ah,

74
00:05:09.987 --> 00:05:14.948
Ben, my master monster chef! What do you need?" Ben

75
00:05:14.949 --> 00:05:17.476
put down his books. "I

76
00:05:17.477 --> 00:05:21.538
don't think I should be on Kids' Kitchen Showdown ."

77
00:05:21.539 --> 00:05:26.629
"What?" Mr. Icky peered closely at Ben.

78
00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:28.540
"I'm not really good at cooking.

79
00:05:28.541 --> 00:05:30.930
I make mistakes all the time.

80
00:05:30.931 --> 00:05:35.507
If my food turns out well, it's totally by accident."

81
00:05:35.508 --> 00:05:38.955
"Nonsense," Mr. Icky said.

82
00:05:38.956 --> 00:05:41.269
"You have a natural talent, Ben.

83
00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:44.822
And I've already given your name to Mr. Freaky."

84
00:05:44.823 --> 00:05:49.041
By now other students were entering the classroom.

85
00:05:49.042 --> 00:05:51.807
"Good morning, everyone," the teacher called.

86
00:05:51.808 --> 00:05:55.830
"Let's get started."

87
00:05:55.831 --> 00:06:02.027
After Mr. Icky described the morning's assignment, Mog came over to Ben.

88
00:06:02.028 --> 00:06:06.314
"Hey, Ben," Mog said. "I heard you talking to Mr. Icky.

89
00:06:06.315 --> 00:06:09.467
I know how you can get out of doing the show."

90
00:06:09.468 --> 00:06:12.106
"You do?" Ben was doubtful.

91
00:06:12.107 --> 00:06:16.811
Mog was a good friend, but he didn't usually have smart ideas.

92
00:06:16.812 --> 00:06:23.034
Mog leaned in closer. "Cook badly today!"

